{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30099 - PROTEIN:5864",
  "verbalization": "Polygonatoside A is shown to interact with the sialyltransferase CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is a key enzyme involved in the synthesis of sialic acid residues on glycoproteins. This enzyme is targeted by multiple compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide, all of which are implicated in targeting U373 MG, a highly metastatic cancer cell line. The shared targeting of this enzyme by different compounds suggests a potential mechanism of action involving the inhibition of sialylation, which may contribute to the anti-cancer effects observed in U373 MG cells. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Polygonatoside A and U373 MG through the modulation of sialyltransferase activity, potentially disrupting cellular processes critical for tumor survival and proliferation. The consistent targeting of the enzyme by multiple compounds, along with the direct interaction of Polygonatoside A with the enzyme, provides a robust foundation for this relationship.",
